{ "Identifier":       {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "PAF-RSR-V1.6-I01", "AIMName": "1PAF-RSR-V1.6-I01"},
  "Header":           "PAF-RSR-V1.6",

  "APIProfile":       "Basic",
  "OnDegraded":       "Continue",
  "Description":      "Response and Scene Rendering: renders the machine's response - a Text - with an Avatar, the Model to animate, as a Speaking Avatar ready to play. Text-To-Speech makes the Machine Speech; Generative Face Description and Generative Body Description make the Face and Body Descriptors from the Text and the Machine Speech; when a Personal Status is supplied, Personal Status De-multiplexing splits it into the Speech, Face and Body (Gesture) Personal Statuses that make them expressive, and when it is absent the avatar renders neutrally. Speaking Avatar Synthesis makes the Speaking Avatar. When a Scene is given - Audio, a 3D Model or a Point of View - Scene and Avatar Rendering places the Speaking Avatar in it and produces the 3D Model Scene with the Avatar placed and the Multimodal Scene (Audio, Speech and 3D Model Scenes); the 2D alternative (Audio Scene and Visual Scene) is not implemented yet.",

